---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BuyButton from '../components/BuyButton.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

/**
 * One video, start to finish: unboxing through to a blocked site.
 *
 * It carries narration, so unlike the silent loop in step 3 on the home page
 * this one has controls and does not autoplay. A 51-second clip that starts
 * talking on its own is the thing people close the tab over, and autoplay with
 * sound is blocked by every browser anyway — it would have played silently and
 * looked broken.
 *
 * The written steps below are not decoration. There are no captions on the
 * file yet, so they are the text alternative for anyone who cannot use the
 * audio, and they are also the faster answer for someone who only wants to
 * know whether installing is hard. Timestamps let a reader jump instead of
 * scrubbing. If captions get added, these stay: they still do that second job.
 */
const chapters = [
  ['0:00', 'The key', 'What arrives, and what it is for.'],
  [
    '0:04',
    'Plug it in',
    'It mounts as a drive called STICK, carrying one file to open on a Mac and one on Windows. Nothing to download.',
  ],
  [
    '0:12',
    'Install',
    'The ordinary installer for your system. It asks for your Mac password once, the way any installer does. There is no account to make and nothing to sign in to.',
  ],
  [
    '0:26',
    'Register the key',
    'The drive you just plugged in becomes the one that ends sessions. This is the step the whole product turns on.',
  ],
  [
    '0:30',
    'Pick what to block',
    'Apps and sites, saved together as a mode. The one in the video ends up blocking four apps and a site.',
  ],
  [
    '0:45',
    'Lock',
    'The session starts, the app says the only way out is the key, and Instagram stops loading.',
  ],
];
---

<Base
  title="Demo | Stick"
  description="A short video: unboxing a Stick, installing it, setting up a mode and watching a site stop loading."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 pt-16 pb-10 md:pt-24">
    <h1 class="headline text-hero">See it work</h1>
    <p class="text-lead mt-9 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The whole thing, start to finish: opening the key, installing the app,
      choosing what to block, and a site refusing to load. About a minute, on a
      Mac.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* Wider than the rest of the site on purpose, and the only section here
      that is.

      The video is 1920 wide but the Stick window inside it is only about 680
      of that — a screen recording of a whole desktop. In a 4xl column the
      video draws at 856px and that window lands at roughly 300, well under
      half the size its text was drawn for, which reads as "bad quality" and
      is really just a downscale. Every pixel of container width goes almost
      entirely into that window. Capped at 1280 because past there a 2x screen
      is upscaling past the source and trading sharpness back for size.

      The prose stays at 4xl. Only the picture wants the room. */}
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1280px] px-5 pb-16">
    {/* preload="metadata" rather than "auto": the file is 9 MB and most
        people who land here have not decided to watch it yet. The poster is a
        still from the video, so the frame is filled before a byte of it
        loads.

        width and height are the file's own, so the browser reserves the right
        box before the poster arrives and nothing below it jumps. No
        aspect-ratio class — that sizes the border box and any padding then
        comes out of the picture. */}
    <video
      src="/demo.mp4"
      poster="/demo-poster.jpg"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      controls
      playsinline
      preload="metadata"
      class="w-full rounded-xl border border-line bg-ink"
    ></video>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-[14px] text-muted">
      Has sound. About a minute.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="rule bg-mist">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
      <h2 class="headline text-display">What happens in it</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        If you would rather read it than watch it, this is the same thing in
        order. Setting one up takes about as long as the video does.
      </p>

      <dl class="mt-10 space-y-6">
        {
          chapters.map(([time, h, p]) => (
            <div class="rule grid gap-1 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <dt class="text-[15px] text-muted tabular-nums">{time}</dt>
              <dd>
                <p class="text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">{h}</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{p}</p>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Windows is the same shape — the installer looks like a Windows
        installer, and the app is the same app. It needs {site.minMacOS}, or
        {' '}{site.minWindows}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="headline text-display">The only way out is a walk.</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      {site.price} plus shipping, one time. Ships {site.shipWindow}.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-9">
      <BuyButton size="lg" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
